From: BCD <190844990+thebcd69@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/metal: Apple frame interpolation and Lossless Scaling for a swapchain's presents

madeira-bcd (X-Plane 12, builds 703 to 706): BCD's Apple frame
interpolation (VideoToolbox's low-latency frame interpolation, iOS 26) and
Lossless Scaling frame generation live in DXMT's present, so a Windows Vulkan
game never got them: on 702 X-Plane drew its menu at the screen's own 120
and its flight at its own 15 with either switched on. With MADEIRA_VT_INTERP=1
or 3 (the app exports it for a game whose own line `vt-interpolation` asks)
wsi_common_metal_vti.m makes the pictures for the followed layer. The game
then never takes the layer's drawables: its swapchain image is copied into
one of three stand-in textures of the module's own (kk_queue.c does not wait
for or signal a stand-in as it does a drawable). At each present the device's
Metal 4 queue signals an event after that copy, a command buffer of the
module's own queue waits for it and copies the picture into a pixel buffer,
and once that copy is done on the GPU its completion handler hands the frame
to a worker thread (in the order of the presents), which lets VideoToolbox
make one or three pictures between the frame before and this one, presents
each from a drawable of its own at its own time, and then the game's frame,
copied as it is; the worker's command buffers go on a second queue of the
module's own. Build 703 let the game and the worker share the layer's three
drawables, and the worker's wait for a fourth held X-Plane at 3.6 FPS; with
the stand-ins only the worker takes drawables. Build 704's worker waited for
each frame's copy in turn, with three source buffers and its output on the
queue of the copies: with X-Plane's flight 130-155 ms behind on the GPU, one
frame in five got its picture; now the worker never waits for the GPU, there
are six source buffers and nothing it presents queues behind a later frame's
copy. The game's thread never waits for the model. Pictures are made only
when the screen can show them and no other frame is ready for the worker; a
session loads on a background queue; three errors, a format or a size the
processor refuses stop it with one line in the log ([vt-interp]
kosmickrisp). The app's in-game menu reaches it through
madeira_kk_vti_set/status/why/session_ended (exported).
MADEIRA_KK_VTI_SELFTEST=1 (BCD's host check) reads back the middle row of
each picture and its two frames and logs where a bright bar is. Without
MADEIRA_VT_INTERP every swapchain is made, acquired and presented exactly as
before.

With MADEIRA_LSFG_HOST_CTL (the app's control file of Lossless Scaling's
frame generation, for a game whose `lossless-scaling` line asks; build 706)
the same stand-ins and worker carry Lossless Scaling's frames instead:
wsi_common_metal_lsfg.m runs the frame generation's chain of passes (that of
BCD's DXMT port, after lsfg-vk 1.0.0) as Metal compute on the worker's queue,
from the person's own shaders, which the app reads out of their Lossless.dll
and translates to Metal Shading Language (MADEIRA_LSFG_HOST_MSL); none of
them is in this library. The frames made are presented before the game's
frame as the pictures are, the control and status files are DXMT's, and
VideoToolbox makes no pictures in such a session. wsi_common_metal_lsfg.m is
GPL-3.0-or-later (its pass chain comes from Porthole's GPL code); the rest of
this patch is MIT.
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_queue.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_queue.c
index a884614..178dabc 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_queue.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_queue.c
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 
 #include "vk_cmd_queue.h"
 
+/* madeira-bcd: src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_metal_vti.m (in the same library) */
+bool wsi_metal_vti_is_stand_in(void *drawable);
+
 struct kk_commit_data {
    struct kk_queue *queue;
    struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd;
@@ -248,7 +251,14 @@ kk_queue_submit(struct vk_queue *vk_queue, struct vk_queue_submit *submit)
       struct kk_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer =
          container_of(submit->command_buffers[i], struct kk_cmd_buffer, vk);
 
-      if (cmd_buffer->drawable) {
+      /* madeira-bcd: a stand-in of the WSI's Apple frame interpolation
+       * (wsi_common_metal_vti.m) is a texture of its own, not a drawable: no
+       * drawable to wait for or to signal; the module orders its reads with an
+       * event after this submit. */
+      const bool stand_in = cmd_buffer->drawable &&
+                            wsi_metal_vti_is_stand_in(cmd_buffer->drawable);
+
+      if (cmd_buffer->drawable && !stand_in) {
          mtl_command_queue_wait_for_drawable(queue->mtl_handle,
                                              cmd_buffer->drawable);
       }
@@ -266,8 +276,9 @@ kk_queue_submit(struct vk_queue *vk_queue, struct vk_queue_submit *submit)
       cmd_buffer->submitted = true;
 
       if (cmd_buffer->drawable) {
-         mtl_command_queue_signal_drawable(queue->mtl_handle,
-                                           cmd_buffer->drawable);
+         if (!stand_in)
+            mtl_command_queue_signal_drawable(queue->mtl_handle,
+                                              cmd_buffer->drawable);
          mtl_release(cmd_buffer->drawable);
          cmd_buffer->drawable = NULL;
          kk_queue_capture_frame(queue, true);
